What the data says
Checkout is the leak. Of 3,854 visitors who browsed, 243 reached checkout, 104 reached sign-in and only 11 completed a booking. The biggest single drop is checkout → sign-in (−57%).
Interest isn't the problem. Visitors browse for 5+ minutes across 6+ pages, with Hotels, Package-Detail and Flights leading. The issue is conversion mechanics, not attention.
Paid channels produced zero bookings. Paid Social (246 sessions) and Paid Search (87) converted nobody, while Organic Search and Direct drove the bookings.
Returning visitors are gold. About 19.5% of visitors return, and they convert 5× better than new ones (0.70% vs 0.14%).
Mobile dominates traffic. 62.5% of sessions are on mobile, 34.6% on desktop.
💡 Recommendations
🔧 Audit the checkout → sign-in transition first. Recovering just 20% of that drop-off would roughly double bookings, with no extra acquisition spend.
💸 Re-evaluate paid social/search spend and track it over a longer window before cutting budget.
🔁 Build a retention / remarketing programme for first-time, non-converting visitors.
🛑 Hold off on top-of-funnel content work. Browse engagement is already healthy.
🏗️ Data Model


A star schema built in SQL, with raw URLs parsed once during staging so the fact table stores only compact integer keys.

                 Dim_Date
                    │
Dim_Campaign ── Fact_PageView ── Dim_Page
                    │
              Dim_Referrer
                    │
        Dim_Session ─── Dim_Visitor



Table	Grain	Purpose
Fact_PageView	1 row per page view (38,097)	Events, with keys to every dimension, sequence in session and exit-page flag
Dim_Session	1 row per session (5,949)	Device, funnel stages reached, conversion flag
Dim_Visitor	1 row per visitor (4,415)	New vs. returning behaviour
Dim_Page	1 row per page type	Browse, checkout, sign-in and booking categories
Dim_Referrer	1 row per referrer / channel	Direct, Organic, Paid, Internal and so on
Dim_Campaign	1 row per UTM combination	Source, medium, campaign
Dim_Date	1 row per day	Calendar attributes, weekend flag
FunnelStages	4 rows	Disconnected helper table that drives the funnel visual's DAX
⚙️ Key Design Decisions
Sessionization in SQL, not Power Query. LAG() plus a windowed SUM() flags a new session after 30 minutes of inactivity, the same default Google Analytics uses. Power Query has no previous-row function and needs an 8-step workaround. SQL also scales to the production dataset (about 1 billion rows), which a single-machine Power Query refresh would not.
Three grains, three questions. Page view (what happened on a click), session (what happened in a visit) and visitor (the whole relationship with the site).
Star schema over a flat table. Smaller and faster for the VertiPaq engine, and each meaning ("Organic Search", "Home") is stored once, not repeated across thousands of rows.
Rule-based classification. Page types are inferred from URL patterns. Channels come from referrer domain plus gclid / fbclid / utm_* parameters. Device type comes from the user agent.
