🚀 How to Reproduce
Load the raw clickstream into SQL Server as WebTrackingData (database: Dnata).
Run Dnata_Webquerydata.sql top to bottom. It profiles the data, stages it, sessionizes it, then builds the dimension and fact tables.
Open Dnata_dashboard.pbix in Power BI Desktop and point the data source at your SQL Server instance.
⚠️ Assumptions & Limitations
Small window. 8 days from a sample of a much larger production dataset, so findings are directional, not definitive.
Very few conversions. Only 12 bookings in total, so channel-level conversion rates rest on thin evidence. The "zero conversions from paid" finding is a signal to watch, not proof.
Data quality notes. 202 page views have CookieID = 0 (kept, as their impact on visitor counts is immaterial). One session shows two "Booking-Complete" views (a refresh or two real bookings; the impact is under 0.02% of sessions). Page types are inferred rather than taken from an official data dictionary.
